From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msi: a package an install has open can still be opened read-only

While a package installs, msi keeps its cached copy (C:\Windows\Installer\
x.msi) open transacted for writing. MsiOpenDatabase(MSIDBOPEN_READONLY) opens
with STGM_SHARE_DENY_WRITE, which a writer already present refuses, so it
failed with ERROR_FUNCTION_FAILED. Custom actions read the cached package:
Java 8's installer.exe, run by its MSI, then crashed and the install hung on
the crash dialog. A read-only open that meets a share or lock violation now
reads a transacted snapshot (STGM_SHARE_DENY_NONE).
---
diff --git a/dlls/msi/database.c b/dlls/msi/database.c
index 292853c..b44c1d4 100644
--- a/dlls/msi/database.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/database.c
@@ -183,6 +183,16 @@ UINT MSI_OpenDatabaseW(LPCWSTR szDBPath, LPCWSTR szPersist, MSIDATABASE **pdb)
     {
         r = StgOpenStorage( szDBPath, NULL,
               STGM_DIRECT|STGM_READ|STGM_SHARE_DENY_WRITE, NULL, 0, &stg);
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_MSI_RO_DENYWRITE
+        /* While a package installs, msi keeps its cached copy open for writing
+         * (transacted; nothing is committed), so a reader that denies writers
+         * cannot get in. Custom actions read that package -- Java's
+         * installer.exe opens C:\Windows\Installer\x.msi read-only and
+         * crashed on the failure -- so read a snapshot beside the writer. */
+        if (r == STG_E_SHAREVIOLATION || r == STG_E_LOCKVIOLATION)
+            r = StgOpenStorage( szDBPath, NULL,
+                  STGM_TRANSACTED|STGM_READ|STGM_SHARE_DENY_NONE, NULL, 0, &stg);
+#endif
     }
     else if( mode == MSI_OPEN_CREATE )
     {
